// An arrangement, built.
//
// BOTTOM UP, and that is the whole design rather than a detail of it. The
// obvious way round is to build the root, place it, grow it, then address each
// cell by path and send it a `hold` — and that version cannot build anything
// the page is not already showing, because a cell does not exist until the
// thing that makes it has answered, and it cannot answer until it knows where
// the cell is. Constructing from the inside out dissolves the question: a
// container is handed its cells as a constructor argument, already finished.
//
// There is no document walker here. Validating a whole nested composition
// against the catalog — unknown keys, unknown components, type fits, RFC 6901
// pointers into the request — is what an agent-facing `compose` tool needs, and
// this demo has no such tool. What it has is a person clicking `+`, which is
// one node at a time.
import {
  "marianoguerra/tutuca/core" @tutuca,
  "marianoguerra/tutuca/demo/universal/catalog",
  "moonbitlang/core/json",
}
